{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(The_simplest_way)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (The simplest way)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Specific)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Specific)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Factoring)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Factoring)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(sol_2_but_fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (sol 2 but fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Not_So_Great_Guessing_Method\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Not So Great Guessing Method</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_Steakmath_(Simplest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by Steakmath (Simplest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfe40a41fdb136435709353d32dbe9a87331a66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(m)=\\frac{m}{2}+\\frac{m^2}{4}+\\frac{m^4}{8}+\\frac{m^8}{8}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"39\" />\nHow many of the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b9168b89260229572428cf2b56143845e44584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf9620bec14e8e3753af9a83f945a188ca57907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab8b20fd6b6ede4e1c9631c23754973953890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f766e01e2a0175965fc00a0a599eefdc5be31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2025)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> are integers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790fd2f1643b47466e5d327bc932fe70d7503210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28The_simplest_way.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(The_simplest_way)\">Solution 1 (The simplest way)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (The simplest way)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b9168b89260229572428cf2b56143845e44584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab8b20fd6b6ede4e1c9631c23754973953890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> must be integers since they are both divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Then let’s consider the remaining two numbers. Since they are not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the result of the first term must be a certain number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95000f89ce1ef8da6c898e51bca3731c8756e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The divisibility rule for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> states that the last two digits of the number must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and we know that the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e14cd7b66034a49310ca061a5e9b42bbf3e9435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2023}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> are the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58ee82f811d0e2994ccd3694be4c262cac79bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${23}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> greater than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the result of the second term must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, the remaining two terms must each be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8173b1c83466f91489ffdcc26ba8fdd4ee59da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf9620bec14e8e3753af9a83f945a188ca57907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f766e01e2a0175965fc00a0a599eefdc5be31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2025)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> are also integers.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2062136270c92a19d30584417a5132b6975a975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Athmyx &amp; mayowl\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Specific.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Specific)\">Solution 2 (Specific)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Specific)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take everything modulo 8 and re-write the entire fraction with denominator 8. This means that we're going to transform the fraction as follows&#160;: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfe40a41fdb136435709353d32dbe9a87331a66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(m)=\\frac{m}{2}+\\frac{m^2}{4}+\\frac{m^4}{8}+\\frac{m^8}{8}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"39\" />\nbecomes \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/2653980077b24355be0c633c3ce914da8ede78b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(m)=\\frac{4m + 2m^2 + m^4 + m^8}{8}\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"39\" />\nAnd in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff8348b511005a0c641105c61b322a05d80704b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> to be an integer, it's important to note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a53af627336ab55171752e3a58e5c2c9db607f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4m + 2m^2 + m^4 + m^8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" /> must be congruent to 0 modulo 8. \nMoreover, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7522304af76b2dc9d8fcf3e2a892d3b0f77160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022 \\equiv 6 \\pmod 8, 2023 \\equiv 7 \\pmod 8, 2024 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8, 2025 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"594\" height=\"20\" />. We can verify it by taking everything modulo 8&#160;: \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545fcbca09ed9678fa7e93c25ef63d384c3b5d7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bba87a538f9c5b4e4ba819ba663f41375336592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(6) + 2(4) + 0 + 0 = 24 + 8 = 32 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"20\" /> -&gt; TRUE\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e83a06b28d1df033ed8ed7312c8114ac00b84e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f3ce8b3206d07c70eb5984857644b9b210f481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(7) + 2(1) + 1 + 1 = 28 + 2 + 1 + 1 = 32 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"436\" height=\"20\" /> -&gt; TRUE\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be953327c758034d54f580b4ed27933cc9f3adda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, then it is obvious that the entire expression is divisible by 8. Therefore, it is true. \nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba4cf9e02d2ac44377e02a7ee46f94d78ca1298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a1570aa28673ed700bb65fbe0a0d27445274c520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/77474929ce25265a19d6c8f60c2859509c795931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(1) + 2(1) + 1 + 1 = 8 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" /> -&gt; TRUE\nTherefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2062136270c92a19d30584417a5132b6975a975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> possible values. \n</p><p>Addendum for certain China test papers&#160;: \nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cffcc060217d17d3dfac1ee9df73da87b346db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026 \\equiv 2 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, taking everything modulo 8, whilst still maintaining the original expression, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba002f4e8403489e284e59f8efd253b93bf5f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(2) + 2(4) + 0 + 0 = 16 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"299\" height=\"20\" />. This is true. \n</p><p>~elpianista227\n~ Major Edits by TrigoEinstein and Co.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Factoring.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Factoring)\">Solution 3 (Factoring)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Factoring)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite the expression as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac9bbaa3b0d97a442d876acefb21b3580189895.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot m \\cdot (m^7+m^3+2m+4).\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is even, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> gives a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/4205135389f2fd4e334cbb5b310cfd4d98745fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^7+m^3+2m+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> will give a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4054552638cf9f29e857a1306bd3ec31df3c19b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> so the result will be an integer. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then notice that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812373100c4b2159e778f6522468140fb9ed99d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2\\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b31db89f02874f7e6389a9d793c719e863ef3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^7+m^3+2m+4\\equiv m+m+2m+4 \\equiv 4(m+1) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"512\" height=\"21\" /> So any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> will result in an integer, meaning the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2062136270c92a19d30584417a5132b6975a975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-nevergonnagiveup\n</p><p>~flyingkinder123 (minor edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking a closer look at the terms, we notice that each term builds off of the previous one. There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0bf3e677cef54ad0b8bb4d05d4d36d43e0e1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed28c07e6560b8707ae41f45678ed0fc219edde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m^{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"41\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e5900bbfc2b254b7419e1f4ba1e78c3a8e5af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{m}{2}\\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d686bb24e43ba860248ccf6e7d0365186795d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m^{4}}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"41\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c26fa30182e4106a64ebdd555f918004e1299b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(\\frac{m^{2}}{4}\\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4caf6ae06f847b10272d940a9eeb2d01701cb9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m^{8}}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"41\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c804ef9f88353afe8e6037e8dc437295a360ef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\left(\\frac{m^{4}}{8}\\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />. Ultimately, this means that there are only two cases that we need to check for: the case in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is even and the case in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is even, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0bf3e677cef54ad0b8bb4d05d4d36d43e0e1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> will be an integer, which means the rest of the terms will be an integer. This means in the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b9168b89260229572428cf2b56143845e44584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab8b20fd6b6ede4e1c9631c23754973953890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> will yield an integer result. (For certain Chinese versions, this also proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8ae4ac803dc46668af2a3fc2ccfe8c4b1db5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2026)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> is an integer.)\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0bf3e677cef54ad0b8bb4d05d4d36d43e0e1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> will result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Building off of each term will give you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, and summing those up will grant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, an integer. This means in the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf9620bec14e8e3753af9a83f945a188ca57907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f766e01e2a0175965fc00a0a599eefdc5be31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2025)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> will also result in integer answers.\n</p><p>In general, all integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> will make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff8348b511005a0c641105c61b322a05d80704b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> give an integer answer, but for this question, this will get us to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2062136270c92a19d30584417a5132b6975a975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> integer values (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b550ea898565bf5504023d5616222edd82b3a267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> for certain Chinese versions of the test).\n</p><p>~unpogged\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28sol_2_but_fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(sol_2_but_fast)\">Solution 5 (sol 2 but fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (sol 2 but fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b9168b89260229572428cf2b56143845e44584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab8b20fd6b6ede4e1c9631c23754973953890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> both work. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261de5c3b8f3697ba3ec2043cf99c6010d193731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023 \\equiv -1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a1570aa28673ed700bb65fbe0a0d27445274c520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. Restating the problem, we have the equation equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5f261bf30c9d68ea8223cda8e4971766269dd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4m+2m^2 + m^4 + m^8}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"177\" height=\"41\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d4d288a994505787ed18fd2edcb86b6f85587d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f422bbc9fa09619a848d53f547bb2688822cd54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4+2+1+1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf9620bec14e8e3753af9a83f945a188ca57907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> works. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b5800f5ad040d308609190ef18a9e0ca08a9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b62a57b9e4cec382700ad7cbe2710682132a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+2+1+1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" /> as well, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f766e01e2a0175965fc00a0a599eefdc5be31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2025)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> also works. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~martianrunner\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/8252d729c71a4b16f2f90f3a8f2e4a4a65365b27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022 \\equiv  0\\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a852d686e9175debe363eb9c3abd503a554d685f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26385497b3b3a0782fe37c476c67ff093f471ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2\\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a23019554cffed4381efb1c35bd6e677a700d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/2860862b98b78ff5ffc7b4e8d794b600ade5fc7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(m) = \\frac{2022}{2} + \\frac{2022^2}{4} + \\frac{2022^4}{8} + \\frac{2022^8}{8} \\equiv \\frac{0}{2} + \\frac{2^2}{4} + \\frac{(-2)^4}{8} + \\frac{(-2)^8}{8} \\equiv \\frac{0}{8} + \\frac{8}{8} + \\frac{16}{8} + \\frac{256}{8} \\equiv \\frac{280}{8} \\equiv 0\\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"874\" height=\"41\" /> meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3edcddbd8511abee9115a07f95453fa94df3233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)|8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> and thus is an integer. \n</p><p>Repeating this process for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c589e143fc32f8c41add16f9872b7fdb54ddf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2023, 2024,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> shows that they're all integers, giving a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/145ccf2da4023f94948f54d275b67b45d7bfd9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) 4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~pandapower24\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On certain versions of the AMC in China, the problem was restated as follows: \n</p><p>Let<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfe40a41fdb136435709353d32dbe9a87331a66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(m)=\\frac{m}{2}+\\frac{m^2}{4}+\\frac{m^4}{8}+\\frac{m^8}{8}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"39\" />How many of the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b9168b89260229572428cf2b56143845e44584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf9620bec14e8e3753af9a83f945a188ca57907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab8b20fd6b6ede4e1c9631c23754973953890b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2024)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d720ab60dcdc4eae79d095e3ff64ab9acc5dfd99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2025),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8ae4ac803dc46668af2a3fc2ccfe8c4b1db5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2026)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> are integers?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b996dd2a41b8bc10a8c09aba149293def2afa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>By identical reasoning, each term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is even. \n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b550ea898565bf5504023d5616222edd82b3a267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~IHateGeometry, countmath1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Not_So_Great_Guessing_Method\">Not So Great Guessing Method</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Not So Great Guessing Method\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this is Question <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> AMC <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />B. It follows that the answer should be something to do with 2024. Option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2062136270c92a19d30584417a5132b6975a975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> is the closest one with the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, if you have no way to solve this and have no clue why you decided to take the AMC, use this method.(Like me!)\n</p><p>~Aggrava\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Xn1JLzT7mW4?si=borSg8xrYLAz7mNY\">https://youtu.be/Xn1JLzT7mW4?si=borSg8xrYLAz7mNY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DOm3Yc6I8sM?si=252mdbZelYqDYVbj\">https://youtu.be/DOm3Yc6I8sM?si=252mdbZelYqDYVbj</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_Steakmath_.28Simplest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_Steakmath_(Simplest)\">Video Solution 3 by Steakmath (Simplest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by Steakmath (Simplest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jWpCw9adStQ\">https://youtu.be/jWpCw9adStQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan